===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|id|ms|buku}}, from {{der|id|nl|boek}}, from {{der|id|dum|boec}}, from {{der|id|odt|buoc}}, from {{der|id|gem-pro|*bōks}}.

====Noun====
{{id-noun}}

# [[book]] {{gloss|collection of sheets of paper bound together containing printed or written material}}
#: {{syn|id|kitab|pustaka}}
# {{ellipsis of|id|buku besar|t=ledger}}

=====Usage notes=====
Although {{m|id|buku}}, {{m|id|kitab}}, and {{m|id|pustaka}} all translate as {{m|en|book}}, the latter two have more specialized usages. The word {{m|id|kitab}} is used commonly for books relating to religion and law. The word {{m|id|pustaka}} is used commonly in literature.

